{
  "id": "ts_prop_house_straw",
  "name": "Straw House",
  "kind": "prop",
  "_comment": "A house that COLLAPSES, with a window you can see the occupant through. Backdrops cannot do either: ToonBackdrop has no poses and is not a cue target, so anything the story breaks must be a prop. The wall is a FRAME of four rects, not a solid polygon with a painted-on window \u2014 the whole prop draws as one actor after anyone upstage of it, so the opening has to be real geometry or a pig behind it is simply hidden. States are POSES driven by a non-looping `collapse` clip; a non-loop clip holds its last key, which leaves a heap on screen instead of the house popping back.",
